The effective radial quadratic
$Q(r) = E r^2 + k e^2 r - L^2/(2 m_{\mathrm{red}})$: along the trajectory
the radial-energy identity gives
$Q(r) = \tfrac{1}{2} m_{\mathrm{red}}\, \dot r^{\,2} r^2$, so $Q(r) = 0$
exactly at turning points.
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Periapsis at the initial separation]
\label{lem:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_B_2:turningQuadratic_periapsis}
\lean{IPhO2026.Problem1.B2.CoulombScatteringData.turningQuadratic_periapsis}
